drm/sun4i: add the H616 HDMI PHY variant

Taken verbatim from ROCKNIX's 0002-rg35xx-enable-HDMI-LCD.patch, which carries
Jernej Skrabec's H616 display series downstream; this is patch 06/21 of that
series, "Add support for H616 HDMI PHY".

Upstream status: not upstream as of 6.18.44. Jernej's DE33 series is still in
review on dri-devel (v8, "drm/sun4i: update DE33 support"), and his own cover
letter says the remaining patches -- the ones that complete the H616 display
pipeline, HDMI included -- go out only once that series lands. So there is no
6.19 to wait for yet.

What is missing from 6.18.44, and what is not. sun8i_dw_hdmi.c already has
everything the H616 controller needs: the DT node below claims
"allwinner,sun50i-h616-dw-hdmi" first and falls back to
"allwinner,sun50i-h6-dw-hdmi", and the H6 quirks are the right ones. The TCON
TV quirks and the display-engine compatible are already in
patches/linux/0100. The one genuine gap is here: sun8i_hdmi_phy.c knows five
PHY variants and none of them is H616, so hdmi-phy@6010000 would never bind
and, because the DRM device is a component master, nothing else in the
pipeline would either.

The three tables are the PHY's per-pixel-clock configuration -- MPLL, current
control and symbol/termination/level -- for 27, 74.25, 148.5, 297 and 594 MHz,
i.e. up to 4K30. The init function is shared with the H6 unchanged, which is
the whole reason this is 75 lines rather than a driver.

NOT VERIFIED ON HARDWARE. Nothing in this tree has ever driven the HDMI port.
The values come from a distribution that ships them for this SoC family, not
from a measurement made here.
